 "specification": {
  "profile": {
   "base64url": "the strict alphabet without padding, and the canonical encoding only",
   "crit": "a crit header is refused (RFC 7515 section 4.1.11): this profile defines no extension",
   "iatSkewSeconds": 300,
   "integers": "port, iat and exp are JSON integers; 443.0 is not 443",
   "jwksHost": "dns-aid.<zone> or the zone apex, over https",
   "payload": "I-JSON (RFC 7493): a duplicate member name is refused",
   "protocol": "the payload alpn is compared with the record's proto when present, else its alpn"
  },
  "scope": "The `sig` binding of a DNS-AID SVCB record: a compact JWS (RFC 7515, ES256 with a raw 64-byte signature) whose payload names the endpoint (fqdn, target, port, agent protocol), an issue and an expiry time, and optionally the `svcb1` digest of the record's SvcParams. The digest is SHA-256 over the ASCII prefix `svcb1:` followed by the canonical JSON of the non-null params (keys sorted, no whitespace). A reader reaches agrees only when the signature verifies, the endpoint and digest match the served record, the record is unexpired and issued no later than five minutes after the check time, and a key authority the consumer holds (today a pin of the key-set fingerprint) ties the key set to the owner of the zone. All fixtures are synthetic.",
  "sources": [
   "RFC 7515 JSON Web Signature, sections 2, 4.1.11 and 7.1",
   "RFC 7518 JSON Web Algorithms, section 3.4 (ES256)",
   "RFC 7493 The I-JSON Message Format",
   "RFC 9460 Service Binding and Parameter Specification via the DNS (SVCB)",
   "RFC 4648 section 3.5 (canonical encoding)",
   "RFC 6979 Deterministic Usage of DSA and ECDSA (fixture signing)",
   "IETF draft on DNS-based agent discovery, section 3.1.1 (record shape)"
  ],
  "status": "proposal of this repository, not a vendored upstream text",
  "verifierContract": "verifier <case file>: the last stdout line is one JSON object with `verdict` (valid or invalid), `codes` (the reason codes, a set) and optionally `decision` (agrees, contradicted or cannot-tell); exit 0 for valid, 1 for invalid."
 },
